# COLD WAR RENAISSANCE — CW-002E
## Rabin × Černý × Gimbert–Oualhadj × stochastic matrix semigroups
### A decidability phase transition between global and weighted-pair synchronization
Date: 2026-08-22
Status: EXACT REDUCTION / IMPOSSIBILITY RESULT; GENERIC PFA UNDECIDABILITY CLASSICAL

## 1. Why this branch matters

CW-002D ended with a natural optimization problem:

> Find a short, sufficiently probable observation/control word whose stochastic action approximately synchronizes hidden-state distributions.

The automata literature suggests that deterministic exact synchronization can have long but finite reset thresholds; the Černý problem asks for a universal polynomial bound.

The probabilistic-automata literature gives a radically different warning:

- Rabin introduced probabilistic automata in 1963;
- threshold/emptiness problems for probabilistic automata are undecidable in general;
- Gimbert–Oualhadj proved the value-1 problem undecidable;
- leaktight/profinite/Markov-monoid theory identifies important decidable subclasses.

Placing these literatures together produces an exact impossibility theorem for weighted approximate synchronization.

The result is independent of DCSG.

