# 2. Two synchronization problems for stochastic matrix semigroups

Let

\[
\Sigma=\{P_a:a\in A\}
\]

be a finite set of rational row-stochastic \(n\times n\) matrices.

For a word

\[
w=a_1\cdots a_k,
\qquad
P_w=P_{a_1}\cdots P_{a_k}.
\]

## Global row synchronization value

Define Dobrushin row diameter

\[
\delta(P)
=
\max_{i,j}
TV(P_{i\cdot},P_{j\cdot}).
\]

Then

\[
\boxed{
v_{\rm glob}(\Sigma)
=
\inf_{w\in A^\ast}
\delta(P_w).
}
\]

This asks whether all starting point masses can be brought arbitrarily close together.

## Designated-pair synchronization value

For two rational distributions \(p,q\),

\[
\boxed{
v_{\rm pair}(\Sigma;p,q)
=
\inf_{w\in A^\ast}
TV(pP_w,qP_w).
}
\]

This asks only whether one designated pair of distributions can be brought arbitrarily close.

At first sight the second problem appears weaker.

Algorithmically it is much harder.

