# 5. Exact synchronization gadget

Given a rational probabilistic automaton

\[
\mathcal A=(Q,A,\{M_a\},\alpha,F),
\]

construct an enlarged stochastic system with state set

\[
\widehat Q
=
\{s\}
\sqcup Q
\sqcup\{z,r\}.
\]

Interpret:

- \(s\): start state;
- \(z\): target synchronized state;
- \(r\): reject trap.

Extend the alphabet by two letters:

\[
\widehat A
=
A\cup\{\triangleright,\square\}.
\]

## Original letters

For \(a\in A\):

- \(s\to s\);
- \(Q\) evolves by \(M_a\);
- \(z\to z\);
- \(r\to r\).

## Start letter \(\triangleright\)

- \(s\) is sent to distribution \(\alpha\) on \(Q\);
- every \(q\in Q\) is fixed;
- \(z,r\) are fixed.

## Stop/readout letter \(\square\)

- \(s\to r\);
- every accepting \(q\in F\) goes to \(z\);
- every rejecting \(q\notin F\) goes to \(r\);
- \(z,r\) are fixed.

Let

\[
p=e_s,
\qquad
q=e_z.
\]

All matrices are rational stochastic matrices.

