# 7. Undecidability of arbitrarily accurate pair synchronization

By Gimbert–Oualhadj value-1 undecidability:

### Theorem CW-002E.3 — Pair synchronization to zero is undecidable

There is no algorithm that, given a finite set of rational stochastic matrices and two designated point masses \(e_s,e_z\), always decides whether

\[
\boxed{
\inf_w
TV(e_sP_w,e_zP_w)
=
0.
}
\]

The target point mass \(e_z\) can be chosen absorbing under every generator.

Thus even a very restricted weighted synchronization problem is undecidable.

This is an exact impossibility theorem.

