# 8. Stronger fixed-threshold undecidability

The same gadget reduces ordinary probabilistic-automaton cut-point emptiness.

For rational

\[
\varepsilon\in(0,1),
\]

\[
TV(e_sP_v,e_zP_v)<\varepsilon
\]

iff the encoded PFA word satisfies

\[
\operatorname{Acc}_{\mathcal A}(w)>1-\varepsilon.
\]

Hence, for every fixed cut point for which PFA emptiness is undecidable, the corresponding pair-synchronization threshold is undecidable.

In particular, using the standard fixed cut-point \(1/2\) formulation:

### Theorem CW-002E.4 — Fixed-accuracy pair synchronization is undecidable

It is undecidable, for rational stochastic generators and designated point masses, whether there exists a word \(w\) with

\[
\boxed{
TV(e_sP_w,e_zP_w)<\frac12.
}
\]

So the difficulty is not caused only by an asymptotic limit at zero.

Even a coarse fixed target accuracy already crosses into undecidability.

