# 11. Toy example: asymptotic pair reset without exact reset

Take a two-state PFA:

- \(A\): accepting, absorbing;
- \(R\): rejecting;
- start at \(R\);
- one letter \(a\) with

\[
M_a
=
\begin{pmatrix}
1&0\\
1/2&1/2
\end{pmatrix}.
\]

Then

\[
\operatorname{Acc}(a^k)
=
1-2^{-k}.
\]

The synchronization gadget gives

\[
\boxed{
TV(
e_sP_{\triangleright a^k\square},
e_z
)
=
2^{-k}.
}
\]

Thus

\[
v_{\rm pair}=0
\]

but no finite word gives exact equality.

At the same time the enlarged system contains two absorbing states \(z,r\), so its global Dobrushin diameter is always \(1\):

\[
v_{\rm glob}=1.
\]

This finite example makes the two notions visibly different.

