# 12. Literature collision / ownership

## Rabin 1963

Probabilistic automata, cut points, isolated cut points, stability, and stochastic-matrix products are classical.

Rabin already emphasized that probabilistic automata introduce numerical phenomena absent from deterministic finite automata.

## Černý / synchronization literature

Exact deterministic reset words, reset thresholds, and the Černý conjecture are classical.

Jungers' synchronizing probability function also gives a probabilistic-game formulation of deterministic synchronization.

Therefore no claim is made that "probability + synchronization" is itself new.

## Gimbert–Oualhadj

Value-1 undecidability is classical.

## Fijalkow–Gimbert–Kelmendi–Oualhadj

Leaktight automata give a major decidable subclass; the value-1 problem there is PSPACE-complete.

## Blondel–Tsitsiklis / matrix semigroups

Reductions from probabilistic automata to undecidable matrix-product problems are classical.

### Current CWR candidate

The specific reduction

\[
