# 13. Consequence for CWR-BP-101/102

The previous frontier asked for a universal theory of shortest probable approximately synchronizing words.

CW-002E shows that in the unrestricted rational weighted setting this goal is impossible algorithmically.

The search must be stratified by structure.

Potential decidable islands include:

- deterministic automata;
- support/scrambling global synchronization;
- primitive/SIA matrix products;
- leaktight probabilistic automata;
- bounded ambiguity;
- positive/mixing HMM stepping products;
- subrectangular/rank-one word classes.

Thus the correct research program is now:

\[
\boxed{
\text{classify the boundary between combinatorial synchronization and numerically undecidable synchronization}.
}
\]

