# Verdict

The Cold War Renaissance interaction produced a sharp impossibility boundary:

\[
\boxed{
v_{\rm glob}=0
\text{ is support-decidable},
}
\]

but

\[
\boxed{
v_{\rm pair}=0
\text{ is undecidable for rational stochastic matrices}.
}
\]

Even deciding whether a designated pair can reach

\[
TV<1/2
\]

is undecidable.

Therefore no general Černý-style recursive reset-length theory can exist for weighted pair synchronization.

Any useful quantitative synchronization theory must exploit structural restrictions.
